OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking):
- Plotly's internal `el.layout.height` DOM-graph-div property can read as
  JS `undefined` for a period after a second `Plotly.newPlot()` call in
  one page session, even though the actual rendered pixel height
  (`el.clientHeight`) is already correct at that instant (confirmed
  1678px via direct probe, matching max(360, 41*38+120)). This is a
  Plotly-library internal-state quirk (not present in DOM/visual state,
  not an a11y-observable defect) that only surfaced because my first
  height assertion happened to read the wrong property; switching to
  `clientHeight` (the actually-rendered, user-visible dimension) resolved
  it. Not a finding against TC1 — noted for anyone else writing chart
  height assertions against this app.
- The default (non-investigation) `category-trends` template variant
  (web/templates/pages/insights.html, `{{define "category-trends"}}`)
  has no `data-trends-toggle` button even though `applyTrendsCap()` still
  hides rows past 12 in it (RF3 behavior, pre-existing, not touched by
  this diff — confirmed identical on master). This is PRE-EXISTING and
  out of TC1's scope; flagging as a backlog observation only, not a FAIL,
  since it predates this change and TC1's diff doesn't reach that
  template. The route actually exercised by the given ranges renders the
  toggle-bearing `insights-trends-table` variant, so it wasn't reachable
  in this audit's live surfaces anyway.

